<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.1" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xml:lang="en-GB">
<!-- The Watch Below, Chapter 44: The General's Silence. Point of view: Calder. -->
<p><s>Chapter Forty-four.</s></p><break time="800ms"/>
<p><s>The General’s Silence.</s></p><break time="1800ms"/>
<!-- p1 -->
<p>For six days after the crossing <sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> hardly spoke.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p2 -->
<p>She lay at the back of the cave at Crow Scar, against the wall, with her great head on the stone and her one eye open, looking at nothing. She ate when <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub> brought her meat, a little. She drank from the spring that came out of the rock. She didn’t go out. When <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> came up through the frozen Fellwood at night and climbed the crag and sat down beside her, she let him put his hand on her brow, and kept her silence.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p3 · reflective -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">He could feel her through the bronze mark. Something going on in her, all the time, day and night, like a millwheel turning under the floor of a mill. Slow and huge and never stopping.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p4 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Is she ill?</prosody> said <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub>, on the third night. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">She doesn’t feel ill. She feels like she’s listening.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p5 · Calder -->
<p>“I don’t know, little one.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p6 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Ask her.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p7 · Calder -->
<p>“I have.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p8 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Ask her again.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p9 -->
<p>He did. He sat beside <sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub>’s head in the dark of the cave and asked her what was wrong.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p10 -->
<p>She didn’t answer for so long that he thought she wasn’t going to. Then, without moving her head:</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p11 · quiet · Aurveth (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Not yet,</prosody> she said.</prosody></p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p12 -->
<p>On the seventh night, midwinter night, she lifted her head.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p13 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">He’d come up late. It was bitter cold, the coldest night yet, so cold the air hurt to breathe and the snow squeaked under his boots like something alive. The moon was full and very high and white, and the Fellwood lay under it black and silver, and from the ledge at the mouth of the cave you could see the whole of the Marches spread out below in the moonlight: the forest, the hills, the white snake of the river, the island, Greyhold’s long wall far down on the other bank with every window lit, white and steady, as only <sub alias="Harthmeer">Hearthmere</sub>’s lamps burned.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p14 · Calder -->
<p>“They’re keeping midwinter,” he said. He’d sat down by the fire <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub> had lit for him in the mouth of the cave, and was holding his hands out to it. “Greyhold. Every light’s on.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p15 -->
<p><sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> lifted her head off the stone.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p16 -->
<p>He felt the slow turning in her catch, at last, and become something else.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p17 · Aurveth (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">I want to go down,</prosody> she said.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p18 -->
<p>He looked at her.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p19 · quiet · Aurveth (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Not to the island. I will not set foot on that island. Not yet.</prosody> She was getting up onto her feet, her scarred back stiff in the cold. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Near it. On the river. Where I can feel.</prosody> She turned her head and looked at him with her one eye. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Will you come with me? I would rather not go alone.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p20 · Lisska (bond, to Aurveth) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Can we come?</prosody> said <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub> at once.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p21 · Aurveth (bond, to Lisska) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">No, child. You and <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> will stay on the hill above his farm and watch. If anything moves on the far bank, a boat, a torch, anything, you will call him.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p22 · Kharrak (bond, to Aurveth) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">What are you going to feel?</prosody> said <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>, from the cave mouth. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">What’s there?</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p23 -->
<p><sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> didn’t answer him either.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p24 -->
<p>She went down off the ledge an hour before midnight, with <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub> flat on her neck behind her head and his arms round the ridge between the plates.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p25 · awe: low silent flight -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">She went low. Lower than he’d ever flown with her. She came off the crag and dropped straight down to the Fellwood and went along over the top of it so low that her belly brushed the snow off the highest branches, and the trees went by under him in the dark, silver and black, a hand’s breadth below. He could hear the snow falling off them behind her in long soft rushes. She went west along the top of the forest, low and silent, with her great wings barely moving, like an owl along a hedge.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p26 -->
<p>Over the shoulder of the hill. Over his own top field, white, with the black ring of the burned stubble under the snow. Down past the Fenn farm, dark and empty. Out over the edge of the land, and down, onto the river.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p27 -->
<p>She landed on the ice a league above the island, under the <sub alias="Salt-reach">Saltreach</sub> bank.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p28 · tension -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">He’d never have found the place. She’d picked it from the air. A long reach of the river where the bank came down steep and high on the east side, with a hanging wood on top of it, so that the bank threw a deep black shadow out across the ice under the high moon. No tower on the <sub alias="Harthmeer">Hearthmere</sub> side could see into it. No window at Greyhold. They came down out of the dark into the shadow with her wings spread wide, and her great feet touched the snow on the ice, and then her weight, and the ice groaned, a long deep sound that went away across the river and came back.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p29 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">And held.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p30 -->
<p>She lowered her neck, and he slid down off it onto the ice.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p31 -->
<p>He’d stood on the river before, crossing to the island. It was different, standing on it beside her. She was so heavy. He could feel the ice bearing her through the soles of his boots. Every time she shifted, a small deep creak went away from her across the river in all directions, like rings going out across a pond.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p32 -->
<p>The island lay downriver, a league off, a long dark shape in the white with the stump of its tower against the sky. She didn’t look at it. She looked down. At the ice under her feet.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p33 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">She lay down flat. All of her. Her belly on the ice, her great wings spread out on either side of her across the snow like two dark sails laid down to dry, her tail out straight behind. She stretched her long neck out along the ice in front of her, and laid her jaw on it, and then turned her head a little, and pressed her throat down against the ice, as a man lies down in a field with his ear to the ground to hear if horses are coming.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p34 -->
<p>She lay like that.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p35 -->
<p>He stood beside her in the black shadow under the bank and waited.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p36 -->
<p>It came up into her slowly.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p37 -->
<p>He felt what it did to her, if not all of what she felt. Through the bronze mark, faint at first, and then stronger, like cold coming up into your feet from the ground when you stand too long.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p38 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">Something below.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p39 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">Below the ice. Below the river. Below the riverbed, and the gravel and the clay under that, and the rock under that. Further down than anything he could think about. He felt her reach down into it, through her throat pressed against the ice. And he felt her touch it.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p40 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">Vast.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p41 · awe: overwhelming size -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">It came up through the mark into him, and it was so big that he put his hand out and leaned on her flank to stay standing. Bigger than her. Bigger than the island. Bigger than <sub alias="Cold-tarn">Coldtarn</sub>, bigger than the <sub alias="Scar-fell">Scarfell</sub>, so big that his head gave up trying to hold the size of it. Lying down there. Under everything. Awake, as surely as the lion on the path under the oaks had been awake, and turning over and over in a bed it couldn’t get out of.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p42 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">And bound.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p43 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">He didn’t have a word for it. He felt it through her like a rope too tight round a beast’s leg, when you put your hand on the beast: the pressure, the place where something is held that shouldn’t be held. Bound, down there in the dark, with something round it, and the something had been there so long that the thing it held had grown round it, like a tree round a nail.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p44 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">Under all of that there was something worse. It came up through the bronze mark into him for one moment, the last thing, the deepest, and it was like nothing he’d ever felt from any beast or any man. It was like a bone set badly. A leg broken and healed crooked, that walks, and carries weight, and is wrong all the way through, every step it takes.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p45 -->
<p>He took his hand off her flank and stood on the ice and was sick.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p46 -->
<p>When he could stand again she hadn’t moved.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p47 -->
<p>She lay flat on the ice with her throat pressed down and her wings spread, and her one eye was open and staring at nothing. What he felt in her was what he’d felt on the hill above the Fenn farm, when she smelled the lion on his coat and put her head down in the snow. The old thing, turning over, very deep. Only now it had stopped turning, and was awake in her.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p48 · Calder -->
<p>“<sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub>,” he said.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p49 -->
<p>Nothing.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p50 · Calder -->
<p>“<sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub>. What is it? What’s down there?”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p51 -->
<p>He felt the question go into her, down through the mark, and land. He felt her close round it, like a hand closing over something small so nobody can see it.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p52 · quiet: very quiet · Aurveth (bond, to Calder), very quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">Do not ask me,</prosody> she said.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p53 -->
<p>Her voice was very quiet, like his mother’s when she was very angry or very frightened and didn’t want him to know which.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p54 · quiet · Aurveth (bond, to Calder), very quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">Not yet. I will tell you when I can bear to.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p55 -->
<p>It went into him and stuck, like a burr in wool.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p56 -->
<p>They stayed on the ice for most of the night.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p57 -->
<p>She didn’t get up. He sat down in the snow beside her head, against the curve of her jaw, where it was warm, and pulled his coat round him and waited. He didn’t ask again. He put his hand on her jaw and left it there.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p58 -->
<p>On the hill above the Fenn farm, a league and a half away, he could feel the other two. Watching. Close enough to talk.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p59 · quiet: whispering · Lisska (bond, to Calder), whispered -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">What’s she doing?</prosody> said <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub>. Whispering, as if they might hear her at Greyhold. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">She feels so heavy. Like she’s carrying something. Is she?</prosody></prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p60 · Calder -->
<p>“I think so.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p61 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">What did she find?</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p62 · Calder -->
<p>“She won’t say.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p63 · Kharrak (bond, to Calder), calmly -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Then I’ll go and dig it up,</prosody> said <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p64 · tension: calm, no anger · Kharrak (bond, to Calder), calmly -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">He said it calmly. That was what made <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>’s head come up: no red tide at all. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Whatever’s down there. Under the island. I can dig. I’ll dig down through the island and see what it is, and then she won’t have to say.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p65 -->
<p><sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> lifted her head off the ice.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p66 -->
<p>It was the first time she’d moved in an hour. She turned it on her long neck and looked up through the dark toward the hill where <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> lay, a league and a half off, as if she could see him.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p67 · anger: very quiet menace · Aurveth (bond, to Kharrak), very quietly -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">If you put one claw into that island,</prosody> she said, very quietly, <prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">I will break your wing myself. The good one. And I will hold you down while it heals crooked.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p68 · tension -->
<p><prosody rate="97%">The hill went silent.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p69 -->
<p>He felt <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub> hear it, and go still, and stay still. He felt <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub> go small and flat in the snow beside <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p70 -->
<p><sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> laid her head back down on the ice.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p71 · grief: frightened, apologetic · Aurveth (bond, to all three) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%"><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">I am sorry,</prosody> she said, after a while. To all of them. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">I have never been frightened like this. Not when Ragnald died. Not when <sub alias="Siggroon">Sigrun</sub> died. Not when the field was burning and I was going out from the edges in. Leave it alone. All of you. Please. Until I understand it.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p72 -->
<p>Nobody answered her.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p73 -->
<p>At midnight the singing came across the ice.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p74 -->
<p>He heard it first as nothing. A change in the air. Then a sound, so faint he thought it was the blood in his ears, or the wind in the hanging wood on the bank above. A long low sound, rising and falling. Coming from downriver, from beyond the island, where Greyhold’s long wall stood on the <sub alias="Harthmeer">Hearthmere</sub> bank with every window lit.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p75 · awe -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">Voices. Hundreds of them. Singing.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p76 -->
<p>He’d never heard anything carry so far. Four leagues and more, across the frozen river, on the still bitter air, with no wind and no water moving to stop it. It came to him thin and very clear, like a voice heard across a valley in the early morning.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p77 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">They’re singing,</prosody> said <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub>, on the hill. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">The knights. On the wall. All of them. It’s the same words over and over.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p78 · Calder -->
<p>“I can’t make out the words.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p79 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">I can. My ears are better than yours.</prosody> She was quiet a moment, listening. She said them to him one at a time, in her small bright voice, keeping time with the far singing:</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p80 · awe: sung words relayed · Lisska (verse), keeping time with the far singing -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="90%">Keep. The watch. Below.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p81 · awe · Lisska (verse), keeping time with the far singing -->
<p><prosody rate="95%"><prosody rate="90%">And do not ask.</prosody></prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p82 -->
<p>Beside him on the ice, <sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> shuddered.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p83 · dread -->
<p><prosody rate="96%">It went through her from the tip of her nose to the end of her tail. The ice under her groaned with it, a long deep sound going out across the river in rings. Her wings, spread out on the snow, pulled in against her sides all at once, like a bird’s when a hawk goes over.</prosody></p><break time="800ms"/>
<!-- p84 · Ada (remembered) -->
<p>He sat in the snow beside her with his hand on her jaw and the singing coming across the ice. He thought of the carving over the arch, that <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub> could see and <sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> could read, and wouldn’t. He thought of his mother at <sub alias="Bell">Bel</sub>’s table, with her face gone the colour of ash. <prosody volume="-3dB">Don’t ask me again, <sub alias="Cawlder">Calder</sub>.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p85 -->
<p>The singing stopped.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p86 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">It stopped all at once, as if a door had shut. The huge frozen silence of the river came back across the ice.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p87 -->
<p><sub alias="Orveth">Aurveth</sub> didn’t lift her head again until the sky went grey in the east.</p>
<break time="1600ms"/><!-- scene break -->
<!-- p88 -->
<p>When she did, she got up off the ice without a word, stiffly, the frost cracking off her scales. She lowered her neck for him. He climbed up behind her head and found the ridge and held on, and she went up off the river into the dawn, low, along the top of the white Fellwood.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p89 -->
<p>She didn’t go to the Scar. She put him down in the snow at the top of <sub alias="Bell">Bel</sub>’s hollow, at the edge of the trees, and when he’d slid off she went on east alone, low over the forest, and didn’t look back.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p90 -->
<p>He stood in the snow and felt the other two coming home behind her.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p91 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">What do we tell them?</prosody> said <sub alias="Liska">Lisska</sub>. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Your mother. <sub alias="Bell">Bel</sub>. When they ask where you went.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p92 -->
<p>He looked down the hollow at the house. Smoke from the chimney, going straight up. Ada would be up. She was always up.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p93 · Calder -->
<p>“Nothing,” he said.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p94 · Lisska (bond, to Calder) -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-2dB">Nothing?</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p95 · urgent: steadier than expected · Calder -->
<p><prosody rate="105%">“Nothing about tonight. Not to Ma. Not to <sub alias="Bell">Bel</sub>, or Fisk, or Wren. Not to anybody.” It came out steadier than he’d thought it would. “And nobody goes near that island. Not a claw on it. Not till she says.”</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p96 -->
<p>The forest was quiet. Then <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>, far off, low.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p97 · Kharrak (bond, to Calder), low, far off -->
<p><prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">I heard her,</prosody> said <sub alias="Karrak">Kharrak</sub>. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">I heard you.</prosody> A pause. <prosody rate="94%" volume="-6dB">I won’t.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p98 -->
<p>He went down the hollow and in at the kitchen door.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p99 -->
<p>Ada was at the hearth with her hand on the warm stone, saying the hearth-words over the banked fire. She finished them before she looked round. She always did. Then she looked at him: at the frost in his hair, and the sick down the front of his coat, and his face.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p100 · Ada -->
<p>“You’ve been out all night,” she said.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p101 · Calder -->
<p>“Yes.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p102 · Ada -->
<p>“Where?”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p103 · Calder -->
<p>“On the river.”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p104 · Ada -->
<p>“And what’s on the river?”</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p105 -->
<p>He thought of it. Lying down there under everything, awake, bound, wrong like a bone set badly.</p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p106 · quiet · Calder -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">“Ice,” he said.</prosody></p><break time="500ms"/>
<!-- p107 · quiet -->
<p><prosody rate="95%">His mother looked at him for a long moment. Then she turned back to the fire and put another log on it, and didn’t ask again.</prosody></p>
<break time="1800ms"/>
</speak>
